From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kai Krakow <kai@kaishome.de>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 02:37:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nvkms: forget failed FRL link training when a modeset doesn't
 use FRL

The attribute that tells nvidia-drm that the last modeset of an HDMI
display failed FRL link training reads frlLinkFailures, which only a
successful FRL link training and a probe of the maximum pixel clock reset.
A modeset without FRL returns from nvHdmiFrlSetConfig() before either. So
after one failed training and a working TMDS mode, every later run of
nvidia-drm's hotplug work, which checks every HDMI connector with a crtc,
sets link-status BAD on that working connector again: when another
display wakes up, after every resume, until the sink itself is
hotplugged. A compositor that honours link-status then sets the mode of
that output again each time.

Reset frlLinkFailures when a modeset sets up a head without FRL. Retries
with FRL keep counting, so the limit on reported failures still applies.

No FRL failure was logged on the system this was reviewed on; found by
reading the code.

Fixes: fff1efbe6e10 ("nvkms, nvidia-drm: report failed HDMI FRL link training of a modeset")
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-hdmi.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-hdmi.c b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-hdmi.c
index 011ffcb2..5b045278 100644
--- a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-hdmi.c
+++ b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-hdmi.c
@@ -3052,6 +3052,19 @@ void nvHdmiFrlSetConfig(NVDispEvoRec *pDispEvo, NvU32 head)
     NvBool trained;
 
     if (pFrlConfig->frlRate == HDMI_FRL_DATA_RATE_NONE) {
+        /*
+         * A modeset without FRL has no link training that could fail:
+         * whatever an earlier FRL modeset reported for this display is over.
+         */
+        if (pHeadState->pConnectorEvo != NULL) {
+            NVDpyEvoPtr pDpyEvo =
+                nvGetDpyEvoFromDispEvo(pDispEvo,
+                                       pHeadState->pConnectorEvo->displayId);
+
+            if (pDpyEvo != NULL) {
+                pDpyEvo->hdmi.frlLinkFailures = 0;
+            }
+        }
         return;
     }
 
